<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Ścinawa</h1><p class="st-meta">1274 CE – 1365 CE (approx.) · capital Ścinawa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small Silesian Piast duchy on the Oder, split off from Głogów in the late 13th century and repeatedly passed between related princes.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konrad-i-of-glogow">Konrad I of Głogów</a> in 1274, his lands were divided among his sons, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scinawa">Ścinawa</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oder-river">Oder</a>, with its surrounding district, became the seat of a small separate duchy. Its first rulers included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/przemko-of-scinawa">Przemko of Ścinawa</a>, who died fighting in 1289.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of its internal history. The duchy was a modest territory of farmland and small towns between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glogow">Głogów</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Wrocław</a>, ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Silesian Piasts</a> who often held other lands as well, and it passed back and forth within the Głogów branch. Its dukes accepted Bohemian overlordship in the 1320s and 1330s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The duchy was absorbed back into the lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glogow">Głogów</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Żagań Piasts</a> in the mid 14th century, by 1365, and later followed them under the Bohemian crown. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scinawa">Ścinawa</a> is now a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="duchy, 1274 CE – 1365 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">duchy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.05%;width:1.81%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1274 CE – 1365 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ścinawa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Przemko of Ścinawa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polish, German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of Steinau</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1320&amp;focus=duchy-of-scinawa" aria-label="Duchy of Ścinawa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5052 397 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Ścinawa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5372 653L5363 646M5372 653L5330 692"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5363 646h0M5330 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5372 653h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5372 653h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ścinawa. <a href="/atlas?year=1320&amp;focus=duchy-of-scinawa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
